<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick III, Elector of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1463–1525</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Frederick the Wise</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick III, Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, known as Frederick the Wise, ruled the Ernestine electorate from 1486 to 1525. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-wittenberg">University of Wittenberg</a> in 1502, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> taught, and protected Luther after his condemnation, refusing to surrender him after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-worms">Diet of Worms</a> in 1521 and hiding him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a>. He was a respected imperial statesman and was considered for the imperial crown in 1519.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Frederick III, Elector of Saxony" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Friedrich_III._von_Sachsen,_genannt_der_Weise_(Liechtenstein_Collection).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
